      "writtenOn": "2026-05-20T15:12:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure we need this. Since well-behaving host shouldn\u0027t try to do partial unmaps, it seems ok to just rely on those `WARN_ON_ONCE(dma_pte_superpage(pte))` checks to refuse unmapping pages that are within a superpage (while still possibly successfully unmap other pages in the requested range)? That\u0027s not \"perfect\" (as we don\u0027t return an error to the host) but avoids extra non-trivial bug-prone code complexity like this function?",
      "revId": "0a0fcfd067eea584761e62d97691af17ed9a4a15",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
